1
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:04,079
Chapter 43.

2
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:10,717
Hark hist. Did you hear that noise? Kabako.

3
00:00:10,718 --> 00:00:15,438
It was the middle watch, a fair moonlight. The seammen were standing in

4
00:00:15,439 --> 00:00:19,758
a cordon extending from one of the freshwater butts in the waist to the

5
00:00:19,759 --> 00:00:24,636
scuttle butt near the taff rail. In this manner they passed the buckets to fill

6
00:00:24,637 --> 00:00:29,199
the scuttlebutt. Standing for the most part on the hallowed precincts of the

7
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:34,079
quarter deck, they were careful not to speak or rustle their feet. From hand to

8
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:38,877
hand the buckets went in the deepest silence, only broken by the occasional

9
00:00:38,878 --> 00:00:45,118
flap of a sail and the steady hum of the unceasingly advancing keel. It was in

10
00:00:45,119 --> 00:00:49,839
the midst of this repose that Archie, one of the cordon, whose post was near

11
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:55,359
