16
00:01:15,119 --> 00:01:21,278
There again. There it is. It sounds like two or three sleepers turning over now.

17
00:01:21,279 --> 00:01:24,557
Kamba, have done shipmate, will you?

18
00:01:24,558 --> 00:01:29,118
It's the three soaked biscuits you eat for supper turning over inside of you.

19
00:01:29,119 --> 00:01:32,318
Nothing else. Look to the bucket.

20
00:01:32,319 --> 00:01:37,679
Say what you will, shipmate. I have sharp ears. I You are the chap, ain't

21
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:42,557
you? that heard the hum of the old Quakerus' knitting needles 50 mi at sea

22
00:01:42,558 --> 00:01:49,278
from Nantucket. You're the chap. Grin away. We'll see what turns up. Harky

23
00:01:49,279 --> 00:01:54,717
Kabako. There is somebody down in the after hold that has not yet been seen on

24
00:01:54,718 --> 00:02:00,557
deck. And I suspect our old mogul knows something of it, too. I heard Stub tell

25
00:02:00,558 --> 00:02:09,398
Flask one morning watch that there was something of that sort in the wind. Dish the bucket.
